TLX-HST.ARC  TLX_HST.1ST

This ARChive contains the following files:

FILENAME       ORIGINAL SIZE    DESCRIPTION

TLX_HST.1ST        2318         - The file you are reading
TLX_HST.DOC        7091         - TLX_HST script documentation
TLX_HSTI.DOC      11011         - Introduction to HST Modem functions
TLX_HSTS.DOC        948         - Telix setup parameters for HST modem
TLX_HST.SLC       26024         - Compiled TLX_HST script (ready to run)
TLX_HST.SLT       54365         - Script SALT source code

All file dates are 12/15/88.  Times are all 7:00 pm.

If the file sizes shown do not match what is in your TLX-HST.ARC
archive, one or more files may have been modified by someone
other than the author (and did not bother to update this
TLX_HST.1ST file).

The TLX_HST.SLT file is the HST SALT script source code. SALT source
is standard CR/LF-delimited ASCII files which contain the
script's programming.  You may view/edit it with any suitable
text editor or word processor which can save files in standard
ASCII format. The compiled script is called TLX_HST.SLC and is
ready to run.  If you customize the .SLT source code do not forget
to use the CS Telix command to recompile the script into executable
.SLC format.

The TLX_HST.DOC contains script-specific documentation.  The
script's operation, however, is very much self-explanatory.

TLX_HSTS.DOC contains a quick description of the Telix configuration
parameters required to operate the HST modem under Telix V3.11.

The TLX_HSTI.DOC file may help you understand more about the modem and
high-speed communications in general, with emphasis on
communications with bulletin board systems.

PLEASE DO NOT Modify or rename this ARChive.

CREDITS: Many thanks to Dan Moore who came up with the original
idea and HST18 script for the QModem comm. package on which this
Telix version was originally based. Also many thanks are due to
Colin Sampaleanu, the author of Telix, for a job well done!

